findings.body:
The guard in `scheduleMemberWelcomeEmailJob` was flipped from `!hasScheduled.processOutbox && !test` to `hasScheduled.processOutbox && !test`. `hasScheduled.processOutbox` starts as `false` and is only set to `true` inside the same block, so on the first call the block is skipped. The function then returns `false` and no `process-member-welcome-emails` job is ever added. Outbox rows will accumulate with nothing to drain them, and no test in the PR catches it because the test environment bypasses this block.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/server/services/member-welcome-emails/jobs/index.js" lines="11-20"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The `NODE_ENV` test exclusion is also written as a double negative. Keep the original form `!hasScheduled.processOutbox && !process.env.NODE_ENV.startsWith('test')` and change only the config check.

::suggestion{file="ghost/core/core/server/services/member-welcome-emails/jobs/index.js" lines="15-15"}
if (!hasScheduled.processOutbox && !process.env.NODE_ENV.startsWith('test')) {

The creation gate in `MemberRepository.create` changed from `labsEnabled && WELCOME_EMAIL_SOURCES.includes(source)` to `welcomeEmailConfig || WELCOME_EMAIL_SOURCES.includes(source)`. When the config is set, which is the testing configuration, every member creation takes the outbox branch, including `import`, `admin`, and `api` sources. The source filter is effectively disabled.

This breaks the PR's own tests. The integration test `does NOT create outbox entry when member is imported` sets the config and expects zero outbox rows. The unit test `does not create outbox entry for disallowed sources` stubs the config to a truthy value and asserts `Outbox.add` is never called for `import`, `admin`, or `api`. Both will fail. Under a real config, imported members and admin-created members would also get welcome emails sent to the test inbox.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/server/services/members/members-api/repositories/MemberRepository.js" lines="340-344"}

